<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22301" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incensum</span></b> , i, n.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A setting fire to</i>, <i>lighting</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hora incensi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. de Virg. 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Concr., <i>incense</i>: incenso imposito, Inscr.
			Fratr. Arv. ap. Marin. p. 639; <i><span class="en">Sulp. Sev.
				Chron. 1, 47, 4</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig.
				4, 12</span></i>: incensum <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμίαμα,</span>
			Gloss. Phil. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In gen., <i>sacrifice</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incensum abominatio est mihi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Jud. 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sap. 18, 21</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id. Ecclus. 45, 20</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
